{"id":"cs-54d4cf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Open-source (MIT) macOS color picker menubar app, built from source on GitHub (no pre-built binaries). macOS 15.8+, SwiftUI + AppKit.\n\n**MVP scope:** menubar app, palettes (named, with named groups), color profiles, picker features.\n\n**Later:** main window app, Smart Formats, contrast checker, color vision simulation, templates, import/export, file-system sync, Color Dock.\n\nProduct spec: `spec.md` (being fleshed out in the child spec task).","labels":["epic"],"sort_order":"a0","title":"Colorsip v1"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:18:50.841653Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Rewrite `spec.md` using the answers to the open questions and the mockups in `design/`, then split the work into feature issues under cs-54d4cf.\n\n## Decisions (from Q\u0026A, 2026-10-14)\n\n**Platform**\n- Open source on GitHub, MIT license, no pre-built binaries (not sandboxed, not on the App Store)\n- macOS 15.8+, SwiftUI + AppKit, macOS only\n- MVP: menubar app, palettes (named, with named groups), color profiles, picker features\n\n**Picker**\n- Global shortcuts can be changed (default Hyper+P). Optional user-assigned global shortcuts for the contrast checker and the main app\n- Cmd+click simulates a paste into the active app (through Smart Formats once they exist)\n- Each pick goes into Color History, and also into the palette selected with the radio button if it isn't locked\n- Holding Option opens a mode popover menu (single / multi / contrast)\n- Loupe shows the value in the selected format plus the friendly name. Esc cancels\n- Contrast mode: pick text color → pick background → open the checker\n- Loupe diameter and grid ranges: agent picks starting defaults, we tune them later\n\n**Palettes and editor**\n- No Color Dock for now\n- The color-wheel toolbar button opens the color vision simulation menu\n- History: last 16 colors, duplicates merged, users can't clear it\n- Locked palette: export only, no other changes\n- Over 16 colors: faded edges, scrollable\n- Groups: one level, made of swatches, each swatch unique within its group\n- Color names: an industry-standard modern dataset (agent picks)\n- Editor color models: HEX, RGB, HSB, HSL, OKLCH, P3. Alpha everywhere\n- Drag and drop between palettes. Undo/redo\n- Palette icons: emoji or SF Symbols\n\n**Formats and profiles**\n- No user-defined format templates for now\n- Smart Formats use the frontmost app at copy time\n- Smart Profiles: app → profile lookup with defaults the user can change. Same feature as \"Color Profiles\"\n- Storage: most lossless and compatible representation (agent picks)\n\n**Sharing and templates**\n- Import and export. Import only the Colorsip format for now\n- Colorsip palette is a document type with its own extension. Modern JSON schema (agent picks). PDF layout: agent proposes\n- Templates are named slots you pick into. Tailwind shades are picked by hand, not generated\n\n**Accessibility**\n- WCAG 2.x and APCA, user selects which\n- Fix buttons on both sides: the user picks which color gets adjusted\n- Color vision simulation applies to swatches only\n\n**Sync**\n- File-system sync folder (Dropbox, OneDrive, Google Drive), plus import/export\n- Everything syncs: on a fresh install, point the app at the sync folder and everything comes back as it was\n\n**App shell**\n- No Dock icon. Launch at login is optional. Popover doesn't detach (open the main window instead)\n- Onboarding detects missing permissions (Screen Recording, Accessibility) and guides the user through them one by one\n\n## Deliverables\n- [ ] Rewrite `spec.md` with the decisions above, including agent-picked defaults\n- [ ] Mark MVP vs later for each feature\n- [ ] Feature issues filed under cs-54d4cf, linked by dependencies","labels":["task"],"parent_id":"cs-54d4cf","sort_order":"a1","title":"Flesh out product spec and derive backlog"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:19:02.828884Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-54d4cf","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Open-source (MIT) macOS color picker menubar app, built from source on GitHub (no pre-built binaries). macOS 15.8+, SwiftUI + AppKit.\n\n## Roadmap\n- **MVP:** menubar app, palettes (named, with named groups), color profiles / Smart Profiles, picker features (single and multi pick)\n- **V2:** contrast checker (including the picker's contrast mode), color vision simulation\n- **V3:** Smart Formats, templates\n- **Not yet assigned:** main window app, import/export, file-system sync\n- **Later / not planned:** Color Dock\n\nProduct spec: `spec.md` (being fleshed out in cs-f1a73a).","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:21:32.727692Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0325559f-da10-45fa-878c-25efd859f0c7","text":"**Roadmap decision (2026-10-14):**\n- MVP: menubar app, palettes + groups, color profiles, picker (single and multi modes only)\n- V2: contrast checker (including picker contrast mode), color vision simulation\n- V3: Smart Formats, templates\n\n**Agent defaults to put in the spec** (the user didn't object):\n- Loupe diameter 120–400 pt, default 200. Grid 5–31 px (odd only), default 11. Both remembered\n- Color names: meodai/color-name-list (MIT)\n- Storage: color space + float components + alpha (CSS Color 4 style). File format follows W3C DTCG, checked with JSON Schema 2020-12\n- PDF: one page per palette, groups as sections, swatches labeled with name/HEX/RGB/OKLCH\n\n**Notes:**\n- `design/` is gitignored, so the mockups are only in the main checkout at `design/`, not in the worktree.\n- E28 (Tailwind shades picked by hand, not generated) is still unconfirmed. It can wait until V3."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:21:36.419618Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-54d4cf","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Open-source (MIT) macOS color picker menubar app, built from source on GitHub (no pre-built binaries). macOS 15.8+, SwiftUI + AppKit.\n\n## Roadmap\n- **MVP:** menubar app, palettes (named, with named groups), color profiles / Smart Profiles, picker features (single and multi pick)\n- **V2:** main window app, import/export, contrast checker (including the picker's contrast mode), color vision simulation\n- **V3:** Smart Formats, templates (Tailwind shades picked by hand), file-system sync\n- **Later / not planned:** Color Dock\n\nProduct spec: `spec.md` (being fleshed out in cs-f1a73a).","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:23:25.277317Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4a7a77e5-892e-490b-b754-cc8510788850","text":"**Roadmap update:** main window app and import/export → V2. File-system sync → V3. E28 confirmed: Tailwind template shades are picked by hand, not generated."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:23:26.248715Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
