{"id":"cs-70c2c3","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:45:27.643345Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-70c2c3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e3e9895f-3ccd-428b-a13e-c922fa274c17","text":"Scaffold implemented. Not committed yet, waiting for review.\n\n**Verified locally (Xcode 26.3, macOS 15.8)**\n- `swift test` in `Packages/ColorsipCore`: 1 Swift Testing test passes\n- `xcodebuild` Debug (ad-hoc signed) and Release (`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`, as in CI) both succeed\n- The built app reports `ApplicationType = UIElement`: no Dock icon and no window. Its bundle ID is `com.nicolas-bettenburg.colorsip`, the minimum OS is 15.8, and the sandbox is off\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec** (now added to it)\n- No `Info.plist` file: it is generated, and `LSUIElement` is set through `INFOPLIST_KEY_LSUIElement`\n- The `.xcodeproj` uses a folder-synchronized group (objectVersion 77, Xcode 16+), so new files in `Colorsip/` need no pbxproj edits\n- Hardened runtime is on but only applied to Release builds. That is Xcode's default for Debug builds\n- The CI workflow has not run on GitHub yet. It runs on the first push"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:45:31.393166Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-70c2c3","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:47:37.20968Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-70c2c3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6735d811-1057-4933-8035-e2dbfbd69801","text":"Revision: I added a **Development practice** section to `CLAUDE.md` with a TDD rule: write tests from the issue spec first, confirm they fail, implement until green, then refactor. Logic goes in `ColorsipCore` so it can be tested. When something can't be tested automatically, the completion comment must say how it was verified by hand. The section sits outside the xpo-managed block, so xpo updates won't overwrite it. I added this to the spec as well."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:47:44.943003Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
