{"id":"cs-7375e5","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:59:45.856747Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7375e5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ba2bd055-193d-4372-9c65-8ac23633a7cb","text":"Implementation is ready for review. `swift test` passes all 37 tests, and the app builds.\n\n**Changed** (`Packages/ColorsipCore`):\n- `Color.swift`: `ColorSpace`, `Color` (storage, conversion, ΔEOK, perceptual equality, gamut check, hex) and `HSB`\n- `Conversion.swift`: the XYZ D65 hub, CSS Color 4 math for OKLab/OKLCH/HSL/HWB, the RGB spaces (built from primaries + D65, with computed inverses), and small `Vector3`/`Matrix3` types\n- `GamutMapping.swift`: the CSS Color 4 binary-search gamut mapping\n- Tests: reference values, all-pairs round trips (1e-9), equality, gamut mapping, hex, HSB, and Generic RGB checked against ColorSync (agrees to ~3e-5, test tolerance 1e-4)\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec:**\n- Hex uses 8 digits only when alpha doesn't round to `ff`.\n- The OKLCH hue is set to 0 below chroma 1e-7.\n\n**Open question:** the app imports both SwiftUI and ColorsipCore, so an unqualified `Color` in app code will be ambiguous once it's used."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:59:49.692265Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7375e5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6c00a262-63f5-4c02-84ab-2530e110e693","text":"Revision: renamed `Color` to `CSipColor` to avoid clashing with `SwiftUI.Color` in the app. Files are now `CSipColor.swift` and `CSipColorTests.swift`, and the spec is updated. All 37 tests pass and the app builds."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T09:01:17.68286Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
