{"id":"cs-5cda46","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b18b08b7-da62-4816-acbe-ed69dd46e9f8","text":"Implementation ready for review (uncommitted in the worktree).\n\n**Core (TDD, 57 tests green, red confirmed first):** `Release`, `PopoverItem`, `MainWindowTab` (release gating), `OutputFormat` (catalogue only), `LaunchAtLogin` over a `LoginItemService` protocol.\n\n**App:** `StatusItemController` (NSStatusItem + transient, non-detachable NSPopover), `PopoverView`, `MainWindowController`/`MainWindowView` (stub main window, Settings tab with Launch at login), `SMAppServiceLoginItem`, `AppModel`. `xcodebuild` builds clean.\n\n**Not in the original spec:** the main window is an AppKit `NSWindow` hosting SwiftUI, not a SwiftUI `Window` scene, because `openWindow` isn't reliably available from the popover. The spec has been updated.\n\n**Manual verification:** status item, popover and SMAppService can't be covered by automated tests. I confirmed the app launches as a background agent with no windows. I couldn't confirm the popover visually from the terminal (no screen capture of the menu bar). The acceptance-criteria checks need a hand test."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T09:20:23.091325Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
