{"id":"cs-86d22b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-45822a6a-eaa8-4126-b680-e215f5b237a2","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n- `OutputFormat.string(for:)` and `CSipColor.formatted(as:)` in `OutputFormat.swift`. They cover every format in the spec table.\n- New `androidXML` case (\"Android (XML)\"). The catalogue test is updated.\n- `CSipColor.byte` is now internal, so Android shares the 8-bit rounding with `hex`.\n- 22 new tests in `OutputFormatTests.swift`. The package has 81 tests, all passing. The app target builds.\n\nDecisions not in the first draft of the spec:\n- Apple formats also gamut-map sRGB-stored colors to sRGB, so extended sRGB values (outside 0–1) don't leak into code.\n- Spec examples corrected: `#3c3cdb` is `hsl(240 68.83% 54.71%)` and `oklch(47.5% 0.233 273.1)`. The \"opaque\" edge case uses alpha 0.9999, because 0.999 is 99.9% with 1 decimal."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T10:04:12.974974Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
