{"id":"cs-06fad2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-168585c5-8d81-41c1-b67a-1207fcbfd7a6","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n- `ColorNames.swift`: `ColorNames` (CSV parsing + static 3-d k-d tree over OKLab, stored in a flat array), `ColorName`, `CSipColor.friendlyName`. Ties go to the entry that comes first in the list.\n- Bundled `colornames.csv` from color-name-list v14.54.2 (31,935 entries) and its MIT license as SwiftPM resources. Confirmed they land in `Colorsip.app` under `ColorsipCore_ColorsipCore.bundle`.\n- README \"Third-party\" section with credit and update steps.\n- `Vector3` gained `lengthSquared` and an axis subscript.\n- 11 new tests (92 total, all green). The k-d tree matches brute-force ΔEOK on 300 random wide-gamut and out-of-gamut colors and on random small lists.\n\nDecisions not in the original request:\n- The user wrote \"14.52.2\", but that version doesn't exist on npm, so I took it as a typo for 14.54.2.\n- Load and index cost in a debug build is ~0.86 s, once, on first use of `ColorNames.shared`. The app should warm it off the main thread at launch (cs-40b6c9). Lookups take ~7 µs each in a debug build (10k in ~70 ms)."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T10:17:28.934741Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
