{"id":"cs-39dff3","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T10:45:58.482074Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-39dff3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6e418725-c034-4da1-8eb3-b982792d622a","text":"Implemented in ColorsipCore (TDD). `swift test`: 164 tests pass. App builds.\n\n**Added**\n- `Library.swift`: `Swatch`, `SwatchGroup`, `PaletteIcon`, `Palette`, `SectionID`, `LibraryError`, and `Library` with all the operations. The operations enforce the rules: no duplicates within a section (ΔEOK), locked palettes can't change, and the pick target is never a locked palette.\n- `UndoableLibrary.swift`: snapshot-based undo and redo with action names. It keeps 100 levels; failed changes and no-op changes aren't recorded.\n- `ColorsipPaletteFormat.swift`: `.colorsip` DTCG encode/decode, plus `Codable` for `CSipColor` and `PaletteIcon`. Timestamps are ISO 8601 with milliseconds.\n- `LibraryStore.swift`: `library.json` plus `palettes/\u003cuuid\u003e.colorsip`. Saving writes only what changed, and every write is atomic. Corrupt files and files from a newer format version are reported and never written. There are generic helpers for `history.json` and `settings.json`.\n- `schema/colorsip-palette.schema.json`, JSON Schema 2020-12.\n- Tests: `SchemaValidator.swift` is a dependency-free validator for the keywords the schema uses. It refuses any unknown keyword and has its own tests.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec** (the issue spec is updated)\n- Your answers: a locked palette can't be the pick target, and locking the target clears it. `formatVersion` moved into `$extensions[\"app.colorsip\"]`; `spec.md` §11.2 is updated to match. Schema validation has no dependencies.\n- Timestamps are rounded to milliseconds, not truncated, so they stay stable through parsing. Every operation takes the time as an `at:` parameter, which defaults to `.now`.\n- Duplicating a palette gives an unlocked \"\u003cname\u003e copy\" right after the original, with new ids.\n- If two palette files have the same internal id, the first one loaded wins.\n\n**Not covered by an automated test:** nothing. The app isn't wired to the library yet; that's cs-a29255."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T11:02:23.064327Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
