{"id":"cs-7f6ead","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-138bf2f7-b37e-44e0-92ed-7111857e1610","text":"Implementation ready for review (uncommitted in the worktree).\n\n**Core** (TDD, `swift test`: 216 tests pass)\n- `KeyboardShortcut` + `ShortcutAction` (picker MVP; contrast checker / main window V2, hidden): key code + modifiers, display strings (\"⌃⌥⌘P\"), Carbon/Cocoa flag conversion, modifier rule.\n- `AppSettings` / `ShortcutBindings` / `LoupeSettings` → `settings.json`. Decoding is lenient per field, values are clamped, and a newer `formatVersion` is rejected. Only non-default shortcuts are stored (`null` = cleared).\n- `SettingsStore`: saves on every change; a corrupt or newer file is never overwritten (`loadIssue`).\n- `ShortcutManager` over a `HotKeyRegistrar` protocol: validation (modifier, duplicate, macOS-reserved), registration failure keeps the old shortcut, suspend/resume for recording.\n- `LocalSettings` (UserDefaults: last pane), `SettingsPane` with release gating; Profiles/Permissions hidden until cs-615265 / cs-0fb394.\n\n**App**\n- `CarbonHotKeyRegistrar` (`RegisterEventHotKey` with `kEventHotKeyExclusive`, `CopySymbolicHotKeys` for macOS-reserved shortcuts), layout-aware key names via `UCKeyTranslate`.\n- `ShortcutRecorder`, `SettingsTab` with General / Shortcuts / Picker panes. The popover format dropdown now reads and writes the persisted default format.\n- Picker shortcut and eyedropper call the same hook, which logs \"Picker requested\" until cs-40b6c9.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec**\n- Type is `AppSettings`, not `Settings`, to avoid clashing with SwiftUI's `Settings` scene.\n- The main window shows its content without an outer tab bar while only one tab is visible (MVP), so the panes aren't nested under a single \"Settings\" tab.\n- README: Accessibility is no longer listed as needed for global shortcuts (Carbon hot keys don't need it); mentions ⌃⌥⌘P.\n\n**Not automatable, please verify by hand**\n1. Press ⌃⌥⌘P with another app frontmost, then check Console (subsystem `com.nicolas-bettenburg.colorsip`, category `picker`) for \"Picker requested\".\n2. Settings ▸ Shortcuts: record a new shortcut, Esc cancels, ⌫ clears, Restore Default; try ⇧P (needs modifier) and ⌘Space (Used by macOS).\n3. Relaunch: format, loupe values, shortcut and last pane are kept; `~/Library/Application Support/Colorsip/Library/settings.json` looks right.\n\nDebug build succeeds with no warnings. I didn't launch the app myself."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T11:25:17.668025Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
