{"id":"cs-0fb394","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-502c733d-f039-41fa-a47c-aefbca874733","text":"Implementation ready for review (uncommitted in the worktree).\n\n**Core (TDD, 241 tests green, red confirmed first):** `Permissions.swift` contains `Permission`, `PermissionChecker`, the `PermissionGuide` value and the `Permissions` model (launch check, `require`, `startGuide(first:)`, skip, close, refresh). `LocalSettings.skippedPermissions` is new. The Permissions settings pane is now visible.\n\n**App:**\n- `SystemPermissionChecker`: CGPreflight/AXIsProcessTrusted. It registers the app with the system, then opens the Privacy pane.\n- `PermissionsCoordinator`: a floating guide window that mirrors `permissions.guide`. It polls every second while open and refreshes when the app becomes active. \"Quit \u0026 Reopen\" waits for the current process to exit before it reopens the app, so the two instances never compete for the global shortcut.\n- `PermissionGuideView`.\n- `PermissionsPane` in Settings.\n- The picker hook now calls `require(.screenRecording)`.\n\nREADME updated.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec:**\n- If the guide's only step (Accessibility) is skipped, the window closes without an \"all set\" step.\n- A test guards that polling with no change doesn't notify observers. Mutating `guide` in place would otherwise reopen and activate the window every second.\n\n**Manual verification needed:** TCC can't be automated, and I didn't launch the app. Please check:\n1. A fresh launch shows the guide.\n2. \"Open System Settings\" lists Colorsip and opens the right pane.\n3. Granting moves the guide on, or \"Quit \u0026 Reopen\" works.\n4. Skipping Accessibility isn't asked again at the next launch.\n5. Settings ▸ Permissions shows the status, and \"Start Guide Again\" works."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T12:50:48.459763Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
