{"id":"cs-a29255","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d6b574ec-8a70-4cdf-909c-92baf5122e36","text":"Implementation ready for review (uncommitted in the worktree).\n\n**Core (TDD, red confirmed first; 261 tests green):**\n- `LibraryController`: loads the library, saves after every `perform`/undo/redo (diff-only), `loadIssues`, `lastError`. After a failed save, the next save writes everything.\n- `SwatchStripLayout`: segment = width / 16, 4 pt group gap, empty sections skipped, `isScrollable`, `fades(offset:)` with 0.5 pt tolerance.\n- `Clipboard` protocol + `copyValue(of:as:to:)`, `CSipColor.displayP3Components`.\n\n**App:** `PaletteListView` / `PaletteRow` / `SwatchStrip` / `DropColorsTarget` in `Colorsip/PaletteListView.swift`; `AppModel` owns the `LibraryController` and exposes `copy` and `setPickTarget`. Load issues are logged with OSLog.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec:**\n- The protocol is `Clipboard`, not `Pasteboard`, because that name clashes with ApplicationServices (spec updated).\n- Clicking the selected radio button keeps it selected; clearing the target is left to cs-d6bd2c.\n- The check mark is black or white depending on OKLCH lightness (\u003e 0.65 → black).\n\n**Manual verification needed:** the popover UI can't be covered by automated tests, and I haven't seen it rendered. The app builds clean (`make build`). Check rows, strips, the scroll fades, the empty target, click-to-copy and Copy as by hand with a populated library."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T14:34:56.865132Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7940c0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Permissions don't survive a rebuild: ad-hoc signing ties TCC grants to one build","description":"The app is signed ad hoc (`CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = \"-\"`). Its designated requirement is therefore just its cdhash:\n\n```\ndesignated =\u003e cdhash H\"f33f98…\" or cdhash H\"dba742…\"\n```\n\nTCC stores a Screen Recording or Accessibility grant against that requirement. Every rebuild, and every copy built in another worktree (each has its own `Builds/Colorsip.app`), gets a new cdhash. The grant then stops applying, even though System Settings still shows \"Colorsip\" checked, because the list is keyed by bundle ID. The onboarding guide shows up again on every launch.\n\nWorkaround: `tccutil reset ScreenCapture com.nicolas-bettenburg.colorsip` (and `Accessibility`), then grant again for the current build.\n\nFix options:\n- Sign local builds with a stable identity, so the designated requirement is identifier plus certificate, not cdhash. Use the developer's own Apple Development certificate via an untracked xcconfig override, or a self-signed local code-signing certificate that the README explains how to create.\n- Document the reset in the README either way.","parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aV","dependencies":[{"source_id":"cs-7940c0","target_id":"cs-a29255","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-14T14:49:12.608557Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-925b95","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Permissions guide \"Quit \u0026 Reopen\" quits but doesn't reopen","description":"`PermissionsCoordinator.relaunch()` starts a `/bin/sh` child that waits for the app's pid to exit and then runs `open \u003cbundle\u003e`. The app quits, but it never comes back.\n\nLikely cause: LaunchServices runs apps as launchd `application.\u003cbundle-id\u003e.*` jobs. When the job's main process exits, launchd tears down the rest of the job, which includes the waiting shell, so `open` never runs.\n\nFix idea: launch the helper outside the app's job, for example:\n- `NSWorkspace.openApplication` with `createsNewApplicationInstance`, with the new instance waiting until the old one has exited before it registers the status item and shortcuts, or\n- a detached helper (setsid via `posix_spawn` with `POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID`).\n\nNeeds manual verification, since this can't be unit-tested.","parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aW","dependencies":[{"source_id":"cs-925b95","target_id":"cs-0fb394","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"cs-925b95","target_id":"cs-a29255","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-14T14:49:16.522628Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f8f139","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Permissions onboarding as one checklist, with at most one restart","description":"The guide walks through the missing permissions one at a time. Screen Recording comes first, and macOS usually only reports it after a restart. So the restart happens partway through, and Accessibility follows as a second round, often with another restart.\n\nReplace the step-by-step guide with **one checklist window** that shows every missing permission at once:\n\n- [ ] Each row: icon, title, explanation, live status (✓ when granted) and its own \"Open System Settings\" button\n- [ ] Accessibility keeps a Skip; skipped permissions are remembered as now\n- [ ] At most one \"Quit \u0026 Reopen\", at the bottom, shown when Screen Recording is turned on in System Settings but not yet reported\n- [ ] \"You're all set\" (or the window closes) once every listed permission is granted or skipped\n- [ ] A feature that needs a permission (`require`) opens the same checklist with that row highlighted\n- [ ] Update `spec.md` §9 (\"walks through them one at a time\" → a checklist)\n- [ ] Core logic (`Permissions` / `PermissionGuide`) stays covered by tests\n\nReported while testing cs-a29255. Relaunch itself is broken: cs-925b95.","parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aX","dependencies":[{"source_id":"cs-f8f139","target_id":"cs-0fb394","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"cs-f8f139","target_id":"cs-925b95","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-10-14T15:18:30.693086Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
