{"id":"cs-7940c0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e9f242be-5a91-472e-a8e8-cecedc4bbc69","text":"Implemented per spec:\n- `scripts/create-signing-cert.sh` / `make signing-cert`: self-signed \"Colorsip Local Signing\" cert in the login keychain, trusted for codeSign only, writes untracked `Config/Signing.local.xcconfig`. Idempotent.\n- `Config/Signing.xcconfig` (ad hoc default + `#include?` local override) is now the target's base config; target-level `CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY` removed.\n- `make build` passes the identity when it's in the keychain, otherwise prints a hint and signs ad hoc.\n- README: \"Keep permissions across rebuilds\" section.\n\nVerification: no unit tests possible (keychain/codesign/TCC). Ad-hoc fallback build verified (cdhash DR). Cert generation + PKCS#12 import verified in a throwaway keychain. Trust step + signed build + stable DR still need a manual run of `make signing-cert` by the user (password prompt). Core tests: 261 pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T15:26:36.682819Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
