{"id":"cs-f8f139","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-598e797a-2d1b-448e-8498-7a2b6146a928","text":"Implemented; ready for hand testing. Build and 265 tests pass.\n\n- **Core**: `PermissionGuide` → `PermissionChecklist` (items, highlighted, skipped). `Permissions` now has `checklist`, `status(of:)`, `isComplete` and `skip(_:)`. `require` highlights its row. New `ScreenRecordingProbe` (pure, tested).\n- **Live Screen Recording detection**: `CGPreflightScreenCaptureAccess() || probe`. The probe returns true if any other app's normal-layer (layer 0) on-screen window exposes a non-empty `kCGWindowName`.\n- **UI**: one window with a row per permission (✓ Granted / Open System Settings / Skip / Skipped). The highlighted row is tinted. Then \"You're all set\".\n- **Dropped \"Quit \u0026 Reopen\"** and `relaunch()`, as the spec allows if live detection holds. If it holds, cs-925b95 becomes obsolete.\n- Updated `spec.md` §9 and the README.\n\n**Not automatable, needs a hand check**: with both permissions reset (`make reset-permissions`), launch the app and turn each one on in System Settings. Each row should flip to ✓ within about 1 s, with no restart."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T15:42:53.380796Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
