{"id":"cs-40b6c9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3e5feba9-c3c7-4c1d-9314-45caa27b143c","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n**Core (TDD, 298 tests green)**\n- `PickerGeometry.swift`: `PickerDisplay`, point ↔ physical pixel math, arrow moves clamped to the display, `PixelGrid`, `PixelSampler` (BGRA), `NativeColor` (display profile → extended Display P3 via ColorSync).\n- `PickerSession.swift`: `LoupeScroll` (wheel = 1 step, trackpad 20 pt/step, natural scrolling normalized), `LoupeLayout`, `PickerSession` state.\n\n**App**\n- `PickerController`: one overlay panel per screen, local event monitor (move, click, scroll, keys), hidden pointer, `CGWarpMouseCursorPosition` for arrows. Cancels if the screen setup changes. Saves the loupe size once on close. A pick copies the value (stand-in until cs-995046).\n- `ScreenSampler`: one `SCStream` for the display under the pointer, own app excluded, color space read from the frame's attachments (falls back to `NSScreen.colorSpace`). Idle frames are skipped.\n- `LoupeView`: nearest-neighbor grid tagged with the display's color space, grid lines, black and white center outline, ring, label capsule.\n- `TestPages/picker-swatches.html` (+ README pointer): sRGB and P3 swatches with expected values computed by Core's own formatters, and 1-physical-pixel patterns.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec**\n- Trackpad momentum scroll events are ignored, so a flick doesn't keep resizing the loupe.\n- Right-click and other keys are swallowed while picking.\n\n**Not automatically testable:** overlay, capture, pointer hiding and warping, drawing. The app builds without warnings, but I haven't run it by hand yet. It needs checking on real displays with the test page."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T16:32:34.548887Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-40b6c9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2557eec2-8b61-4d38-837b-4f4658167c82","text":"**Revision: capture color space and precision** (after the swatch test found #ffff00 → #feff00; other pickers are off the same way)\n\nRoot cause, reproduced off-screen with the built-in display's profile:\n1. Converting sRGB into the calibrated panel profile **clips** (sRGB blue → native red 0.0 → `#1b00ff`; yellow → `#feff00`). No bit depth recovers that.\n2. 8-bit capture through any wider space is off by one for about half of all 8-bit sRGB colors. Gamma-encoded half floats still fail near black (`#03d200` → `#04d200`). **Linear** half floats round-trip all of them.\n\nChanges:\n- `spec.md` §4.2 and §6: capture in extended linear Display P3, as half floats. The \"Display native\" fallback profile is dropped (relevant for cs-615265).\n- Core: `PixelSample` (Double), `CapturePixelFormat` (half / `l10r` / BGRA) with a hand-written half decoder (no `Float16`, so x86_64 builds), and `CaptureColor` (ColorSync to extended P3). The new test `sRGBBytesRoundTripThroughLinearHalfFloatP3` proves the hex round trip.\n- App: `ScreenSampler` requests `extendedLinearDisplayP3` + `64RGBAHalf`, falls back to `l10r` then BGRA, drops frames in an unexpected format, and logs the format and space of the first frame. The loupe draws a float image.\n- Test page: sRGB swatches are now expected to match exactly.\n\nStill to verify by hand: whether ScreenCaptureKit composites before the display profile is applied. If it does, blue and yellow come out exact."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T16:50:09.484152Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
