{"id":"cs-979715","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-709432bb-ed39-42bd-b12e-36bc347f33ef","text":"Implemented with TDD. `make test`: 320 tests pass. `make build` succeeds.\n\n**Core**\n- `ColorHistory.swift`:\n  - `ColorHistory` keeps 16 entries, newest first. Re-picking a perceptually equal color replaces the old entry at the front. `record` is the only change. `init(swatches:)` removes duplicates and trims to 16.\n  - The JSON has `formatVersion` and `swatches`. A newer version is rejected, and bad entries are skipped.\n- `ColorHistoryController` loads and saves `history.json` atomically. A corrupt or newer file is reported and never overwritten. History isn't part of undo.\n- `SwatchStripLayout(swatches:width:)` lays out a single section of swatches.\n- Tests are in `ColorHistoryTests.swift`, plus a new strip-layout test. One test checks that undoing a library change leaves history alone.\n\n**App**\n- `AppModel.history` and `recordPick` (named with `friendlyName`). `onPick` now records the pick and copies it.\n- The `HistoryRow` comes first and is always shown:\n  - A clock icon, then \"Color History\". The strip only offers click to copy and Copy as….\n  - Empty history shows the placeholder \"Picked colors appear here\".\n- The \"No palettes yet\" hint now sits below the history row.\n- Other changes:\n  - `DropColorsTarget` is now `StripPlaceholder(label:)`.\n  - `SwatchStrip` can now take either a palette or a list of swatches.\n- History load issues are logged together with the library's.\n\n**Not covered by automated tests (check by hand):** the SwiftUI row, and the picker → history wiring. To check: pick 17+ colors, re-pick an existing one, then relaunch.\n\n**Deferred:** dragging out of history is cs-c07049, as agreed."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:44:07.725208Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
