{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-29581cec-f5bf-4193-9bf9-7569ab948e35","text":"Implementation ready for review. `swift test` passes (349 tests) and `make build` is clean.\n\n**Core (TDD)**\n- `LibraryCommands.swift`: one named undoable command per menu item on `LibraryController`. Names are trimmed and empty ones ignored; an empty description becomes nil. Failures are no-ops that return `false`/`nil`.\n- `LibraryMenus.swift`: palette, group and swatch menu items as data, plus the delete-confirmation predicates.\n- `PaletteIconInput.swift`: single-emoji validation, curated SF Symbols and symbol search.\n- `Library.movePalette(_:before:)` and `Library.uniqueName(_:among:)`.\n- **Change beyond the spec:** `Library` no longer bumps `modifiedAt` when an edit changes nothing (palette or swatch). Without this, renaming to the same name recorded an undo step and rewrote the file.\n\n**App (to check by hand)**\n- + creates a palette and opens Rename. The row popover (`LibraryEditView.swift`) hosts the text edits, the delete confirmations and the icon picker.\n- Context menus on the palette row and on each swatch.\n- The radio button toggles.\n- Dragging a header reorders palettes, with an insertion line.\n- Hidden Cmd+Z / Shift+Cmd+Z buttons in the popover.\n\n**Not yet verified by hand:**\n- The transient menubar popover stays open while a child popover is up.\n- The new palette's Rename popover appears after scrolling.\n- Header drag-reorder works with the in-process UTType.\n- The Character Viewer inserts into the emoji field."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T22:11:58.160605Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:39:12.364266Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9127de9f-75d9-44fb-a4c4-2673450f2be4","text":"**Review changes applied.** The spec was updated first: decisions 8 and 9, the new acceptance criteria, and the drag mechanics now match the code.\n\n- **Strip height:** swatch strips and the empty placeholder are 32 pt tall (were 20 pt).\n- **New palettes:** `newPalette` now inserts at the top, right below Color History. This was done test-first.\n- **Row cards:** Color History and each palette sit in their own rounded card. The card is white with black text in light mode and black with white text in dark mode. Gaps between cards went from 14 to 8 pt.\n  - The `rowCard()` modifier reads `colorScheme` from the environment. A later per-palette light/dark setting only needs to set `.environment(\\.colorScheme, …)` on one card.\n\n`swift test`: 349 tests pass. `make build` is clean."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:40:27.077015Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:46:33.124202Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-61624bf7-cd15-42b1-87d4-646de434b158","text":"**Second round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decisions 9–11).\n\n- **One container:** the per-row cards are replaced by a single rounded container that holds Color History and every palette. It's white with black text in light mode and black with white text in dark mode. It sits 10 pt from the popover edges, with 10 pt of inner padding, and rows are 14 pt apart. The modifier is `listContainer()`.\n- **Fonts:** row labels (the \"Color History\" title, palette names and emoji/symbol icons) are 12 pt. Placeholder text and the \"No palettes yet\" hint use the body font.\n- **Agent decision:** Color History is inside the container as its first row.\n\n`make build` is clean. No core changes."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:47:00.217966Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:52:55.349397Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-31ab3e23-2bda-4274-8da3-9bf9f72d6731","text":"**Third round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decisions 11 and 13).\n\nClicking a palette's header (icon and name) now selects it as the pick target through the new core command `selectPickTarget`, which was added test-first.\n- Clicking it again does nothing. Only the radio button clears the target.\n- A locked palette's name does nothing.\n- Dragging the header still reorders the palettes.\n\n`swift test`: 350 tests pass. `make build` is clean."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:53:39.348686Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:55:24.291013Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2d415483-af48-4e0c-afe6-ce7aa143194b","text":"**Fourth round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decisions 12, 13, 16 and 17, and core item 7).\n\n- **Popover background:** #E5E7E9 in light mode. The color comes from `PopoverBackgroundView`, which is inserted behind the popover's frame view so it covers the arrow too. Dark mode keeps the system material.\n- **Drag to sort, reworked:** the first version used `onDrag` with an undeclared custom UTType and didn't work in the popover. It's replaced by a SwiftUI `DragGesture` on the palette header, inside the list. The minimum distance of 4 pt keeps a click as a pick-target selection.\n  - While dragging, the row dims to 40% and an accent insertion line shows where it will land.\n  - Releasing calls `movePalette(_:before:)`, which is undoable and saved.\n  - The drop slot comes from the new core type `ListReorder`, built test-first: `insertionIndex`, `isNoOp` and `move`.\n  - The list is lazy, so only rows on screen report frames. The slot is computed among those rows and mapped back to the full list.\n  - The `UTType`, the `DropDelegate` and the `next` plumbing are removed.\n\n`swift test`: 353 tests pass. `make build` is clean.\n\n**To check by hand:** the popover's corners and arrow look right with the custom background, and dragging reorders."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:57:27.764592Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:11:45.645147Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c3194a25-5cec-4be3-a8e1-c269e225b67c","text":"**Fifth round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decisions 14 and 15).\n\n- **Container corners:** the list container's corner radius is now 12 pt (was 8).\n- **No separators:** the two `Divider`s around the list in `PopoverView` are gone.\n- **Spacing:** the list's vertical padding is dropped, so the gap from the container to the format menu and to the bottom bar stays 10 pt instead of doubling. The horizontal margin is still 10 pt.\n\n`make build` is clean. No core changes."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:12:05.568559Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:16:39.218833Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9780f71b-aada-4c58-8971-e00be8939455","text":"**Sixth round of review changes.** The spec was updated first: decisions 16–18 and 23–24, and core item 8. The product spec's §7.3 now describes the new strip rule.\n\n- **Color History:** the clock icon is removed.\n- **Popover height fits the list:** the popover is no longer a fixed 420 pt.\n  - The list's scroll view is as tall as its measured content, up to 300 pt, and scrolls past that.\n  - The bottom bar now sits 10 pt below the container.\n- **Spreading swatches**, test-first in `SwatchStripLayout`:\n  - With 16 swatches or fewer, segments share the width left after the gaps, so the strip fills exactly.\n  - Over 16, segments stay at 1/16 of the width and the strip scrolls.\n  - 8 + 8 in two groups now fits without scrolling.\n  - Color History spreads too.\n\n`swift test`: 356 tests pass. `make build` is clean."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:17:59.875837Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:21:06.005708Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2c9cdee5-ca0e-449d-ae86-cf6d488c8ece","text":"**Seventh round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decisions 19 and 26).\n\nEach strip segment (the ungrouped section and each group) now has:\n- a 1 pt border inside its edge, `Color.primary` at 12% opacity: faint grey on white, faint light grey on black;\n- a subtle shadow: black at 15% opacity, radius 1.5, y offset 0.5.\n\nThe strip's scroll content is inset 2 pt so the shadow isn't clipped. Swatches stay 32 pt tall and the layout gets the width minus the inset. The dashed placeholder gets the same inset, so its edges line up with the strips.\n\n`make build` is clean. No core changes."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:21:30.990079Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:32:10.582079Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b6c84061-8a4b-42e5-a2ef-535a59e8be6e","text":"**Eighth round of review changes.** The spec was updated first (decision 20).\n\n- **Rounding:** strip segments and the dashed placeholder use a 6 pt corner radius (was 4 pt).\n- **Gap between groups:** `SwatchStripLayout.groupGap` is 6 pt (was 4 pt). This was test-first: a new `groupGapIsSixPoints` test, and the fixed-number layout tests now use widths that divide evenly with the 6 pt gap.\n\n`swift test`: 357 tests pass. `make build` is clean."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T07:33:05.000717Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
