{"id":"cs-c07049","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8be9324b-50b3-4f3b-bca5-ea9608f2e6e2","text":"Implementation ready for review (uncommitted in the worktree).\n\n**Core** (`SwatchDrag.swift`, test-first, 406 tests green):\n- `SwatchDragSource`, `SwatchDrag.operation` (move/copy/refused), `isUnchanged`, `payload`\n- `LibraryController.dropSwatch` → `.moved / .copied / .unchanged / .duplicate(existing:) / .refused`, undo steps \"Move Swatch\" / \"Copy Swatch\"\n- `SwatchStripLayout.dropSlot(at:)` and `insertionX(for:)`\n- `SectionID.init(palette:group:)` made public\n\n**App** (`SwatchDragAndDrop.swift`, `PaletteListView`, `AppModel`, `PopoverView`):\n- `.onDrag` on every swatch cell (palettes and history): text in the active format + NSColor (keyed archive under the color pasteboard type, since NSColor isn't `NSItemProviderWriting`)\n- `.onDrop` on strips (with an insertion line), palette headers and the placeholder. Option read from `NSEvent.modifierFlags`; forbidden cursor on locked palettes\n- Dropped text is checked against the expected payload before acting\n- Duplicate → 2 pt ring on the existing swatch for ~1 s\n- `AppModel.drag` cleared on drop and when the popover closes\n- `spec.md` §7.5 updated\n\n**Not covered by automated tests:** the drag session, drop targets, cursor, insertion line, ring and drag out to other apps. These need a hand check in the running app; I couldn't drive drags myself."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T08:55:15.907429Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
