{"id":"cs-722793","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e20cfe30-0936-45ab-ba95-4f1095126413","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n- **Core**\n  - `ColorEditor` / `EditorModel` (`ColorEditor.swift`) hold the draft: working space, HSB state, fields, parsing, auto-name and reset.\n  - `Library.editSwatch` and `LibraryController.editSwatch` / `save(_:in:)` apply color, name and description as one \"Edit Color\" step and return a `SwatchEditResult`.\n  - Also new: `SwatchMenuItem.edit` and `LocalSettings.editorModel`.\n  - 40-odd new tests in `ColorEditorTests.swift` and `EditSwatchTests.swift`. All 445 pass.\n- **App**\n  - `ColorEditorView`; the Edit… menu item; editor state in `AppModel`.\n  - `PickerController.open(repick:)` and `StatusItemController.showPopover()` for the eyedropper.\n  - The Debug build succeeds.\n\nDecisions not in the first draft of the spec (the spec is updated):\n- The editor **replaces the popover content** (it slides in) instead of using a SwiftUI `.sheet`.\n- A refused duplicate **names the existing swatch** in a message. The strip highlight would be hidden behind the editor.\n- Library Undo/Redo keys are off while the editor is open.\n- In re-pick mode, the first pick closes the picker in any mode.\n- The private `Library.editSwatch` helper is renamed `modifySwatch` to make room for the public method.\n\nNot covered by automated tests: the SwiftUI controls and the eyedropper round trip (picker → popover reopens with the draft). I haven't tested these in the running app yet."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T10:01:58.930148Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-722793","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T12:35:46.989594Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-722793","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-96165eb7-40d2-4bd2-bc17-5423be16e4e1","text":"Review revisions applied; the spec is updated first.\n\n- The HEX field's label is \"HEX\" (`EditorModel.hex.fieldLabels`; the test is updated).\n- The alpha field has a fixed 44 pt text field, so \"100\" fits. The \"%\" is gone.\n- The Name and Description labels are left-aligned above their fields. Placeholders are \"Name\" and \"Add a description\".\n\nAll 445 Core tests pass and the Debug build succeeds."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T12:36:34.885863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
