{"id":"cs-4a8aa3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Make swatches in the popover feel clickable and show which color they are.\n\n**Today:** swatches in `SwatchStrip` (`Colorsip/PaletteListView.swift:446`) use `.help(\"name — value\")`. That's the system tooltip, which only appears after a delay, and the cursor stays an arrow.\n\n**Wanted**\n- While the mouse is over a swatch, show a small popover/label with the color's name right away, with no tooltip delay. It goes away when the mouse leaves.\n- While hovering a swatch, the cursor changes to the pointing hand (`NSCursor.pointingHand`) to show that clicking copies the color.\n\n**Notes / open questions**\n- Should the label also show the formatted value (as the current tooltip does), or only the name?\n- The label must not get in the way of click-to-copy, the \"copied\" check mark, drag and drop, or the context menu.\n- Moving quickly across a strip should move the label from swatch to swatch without flicker.\n- Push the cursor on hover and pop it on exit, so a cursor never gets stuck (for example when the popover closes mid-hover).\n- Decide whether `.help` stays alongside the new label (it's useful for accessibility) or gets replaced.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aV","title":"Instant hover label and pointing-hand cursor on swatches"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T12:44:18.121556Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-4a8aa3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Make swatches in the popover feel clickable and show which color they are.\n\n**Today:** swatches in `SwatchStrip` (`Colorsip/PaletteListView.swift:446`) use `.help(\"name — value\")`. That's the system tooltip, which only appears after a delay, and the cursor stays an arrow.\n\n**Wanted**\n- While the mouse is over a swatch, show a small popover/label right away, with no tooltip delay. It shows the color's **name and formatted value** (in the current output format). It goes away when the mouse leaves.\n  - If name + value turns out to be too much in practice, cut it down to just the name.\n- While hovering a swatch, the cursor changes to the pointing hand (`NSCursor.pointingHand`) to show that clicking copies the color.\n\n**Notes / open questions**\n- The label must not get in the way of click-to-copy, the \"copied\" check mark, drag and drop, or the context menu.\n- Moving quickly across a strip should move the label from swatch to swatch without flicker.\n- Push the cursor on hover and pop it on exit, so a cursor never gets stuck (for example when the popover closes mid-hover).\n- Decide whether `.help` stays alongside the new label (it's useful for accessibility) or gets replaced.","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-15T12:45:03.6812Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
