{"id":"cs-4a8aa3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ff01c63a-0267-4ee8-bf27-79f675561ffd","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n- **Core:** `SwatchHover.swift` has `SwatchHoverLabel`, `SwatchHoverTracker` and `HoverLabelPlacement`, covered by 12 new tests. All 459 core tests pass, and the app builds.\n- **App:** a new `SwatchHoverPanel` is a mouse-transparent floating panel. In `SwatchStrip.cell`, `.onContinuousHover` drives it, the cursor is set with `.pointerStyle(.link)`, and `.help` is replaced by an accessibility label. The label also hides on strip scroll, list scroll and popover close.\n\nChanges from the spec:\n- The tracker's `prune` is dropped. The cell's `.onDisappear` covers the case and also handles the editor taking over the popover.\n- After a format change, the value refreshes on the next pointer move, not live.\n\n**Not covered by automated tests:** the panel display, the cursor, and that copy, drag and context menu still work. I haven't checked these by hand yet, so they need a manual pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T12:54:15.047904Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-4a8aa3","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T13:01:23.515392Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-4a8aa3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a2a04920-a18e-438a-92ab-e4309b7e18e0","text":"Revision, as requested:\n- The label is one line: `name (value)`, for example `Dust Red (#3c72da)`. With no name, it shows only the value.\n- After a copy, the label reads `Copied` for as long as the check mark shows (about a second), then goes back. It stays in place, using the new `SwatchHoverPanel.update`.\n- As a side effect, a format change now also refreshes the label live.\n\nI updated the spec. All 459 core tests pass and the app builds. I haven't checked the UI by hand yet."},"created_at":"2026-10-15T13:02:16.916315Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.300 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
